spans.s:
ātmán, m.
 —1. breath;
 —2. spirit; soul
(cf. 84^8N.), as principle of life and feeling;
 —3. self; very often so used as a simple
reflexive pron. [514]; e. g., myself, 36^16;
thyself, 26^15; himself, 4^19; in genitive:
his, 17^16; her, 46^5; one's own, 21^18, 58^22;
 —4. nature, character, peculiarity; esp.
at end of cpds, see ātmaka;
 —5. the
soul κατ᾽ ἐξοχήν, the soul of the universe,
 66^8. [cf. ἀϋτμήν, ‘breath’; ἀτμός,
‘vapor’; AS. ǣþm, ǣðm, ‘breath’: for
mg, cf. πνεῦμα and Lat. anima, ‘breath,
spirit.’]
